      "claim": "There have not been any studies among women taking albuterol while breastfeeding. However, using an albuterol inhaler is expected to lead to low amounts in the blood system and therefore likely low amounts at most in breastmilk. Inhaled bronchodilators have generally been considered acceptable for use during breastfeeding. Be sure to talk to your healthcare provider about all your breastfeeding questions.",
